3. `action`: reportExistingDevBranch throws (non-fatal) → continues. Make cli throw on ls-remote → remoteBranchExists catches → warns returns false... Actually ls-remote failure inside reportExistingDevBranch: remoteBranchExists catches and returns false? prHelper.remoteBranchExists — on cli throw it warns and returns false → returns false. That doesn't throw. To make reportExistingDevBranch throw... hard. Skip — leave branch covered via extraction anyway. Actually with the refactor, `reportExistingDevBranch` call moves into a helper `runExistingWorkReportStep`; its catch is inside that helper. The branch (catch) may stay uncovered but the helper's CRAP will be low.

